<OBJECTS_GENERATION>


/*
================================================================================
RMSTEST_84a - inside a branch that never runs, does a comment word whose
engine number is a control word act as that control word?
Feeds: docs/token-alias-design.md Sec.3.2 and slice C.

The header is at the bottom on purpose and names no constant whose number is
a comment marker or a control word.

THE CASE. A conditional on a label nothing defines, so its branch is dead.
Inside it, a comment holding one terrain word whose number is 6, the number
the RMS Equivalencies sheet gives the word that closes a conditional. After
the comment, a create_terrain painting SNOW over all GRASS.

Already measured, 2026-11-02: such words in dead CODE do nothing in DE. 597 of
them sit in dead text in maps the preview matches tile for tile. This run asks
only about dead text inside a COMMENT, which those maps never have.

PREDICTIONS, written 2026-11-02 before the run.
  - The word acts as the close: the conditional ends inside the comment, the
    create_terrain runs, the map is SNOW, and the real close after it is a
    stray token.
  - It does not: the branch stays dead, the map is GRASS.
Read: probe_scenario.py, terrain histogram. SNOW above 0 means it acts.

Control: 84b, the same with an ordinary lowercase word in the comment.

Generate at: Tiny, 2 players, seed 1000, scenario editor.
================================================================================
*/
